{"name":"Lola","hex":"#b9acbb","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Lola","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from Spanish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Lola"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lolá","blocks":[{"text":"Lolá is a corregimiento in Las Palmas District, Veraguas Province, Panama with a population of 946 as of 2010. Its population as of 1990 was 960; its population as of 2000 was 1,022."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lol%C3%A1"},{"title":"Lola (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Lola\" is a song by the English rock band the Kinks, written by frontman Ray Davies for their 1970 album Lola Versus Powerman and the Moneygoround, Part One. The song details a romantic encounter in a Soho bar between a young man and Lola, who is possibly a trans woman or cross-dresser. In the song, the narrator describes his confusion towards Lola, who \"walked like a woman but talked like a man\", yet he remains infatuated with her."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/aa/Kinks_Lola_Uk_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lola_(song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/aa/Kinks_Lola_Uk_Cover.jpg/250px-Kinks_Lola_Uk_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/aa/Kinks_Lola_Uk_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/aa/Kinks_Lola_Uk_Cover.jpg/250px-Kinks_Lola_Uk_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKinks_Lola_Uk_Cover.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/ee/Kinks_1970_Europe_Lola_Cover.jpg/250px-Kinks_1970_Europe_Lola_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&u